"""
One end of an air hose: absolute pressure across it, air mass flow through it.

Connected ports share `p`, and their `mdot` sum to zero, so the air one end gives up is the air
the other end receives. `mdot` is positive into the component that owns the port. A port left
unconnected carries no flow: a capped hose.

`p` is absolute, as on a `HydraulicComponents` port; a component that works in gauge pressure
holds its ambient reference as a parameter.
"""
connector GasPort
  "Absolute pressure at the hose end"
  potential p::Pressure
  "Air mass flow into the component"
  flow mdot::MassFlowRate
metadata {
  "Dyad": {
    "labels": [{"label": "$(instance)", "x": 500, "y": 1100, "layer": "icon"}],
    "icons": {
      "default": "dyad://VehicleComponents/Interfaces/GasPortA.svg",
      "gas_port_a": "dyad://VehicleComponents/Interfaces/GasPortA.svg",
      "gas_port_b": "dyad://VehicleComponents/Interfaces/GasPortB.svg"
    },
    "path": {"stroke": "#00897b"}
  }
}
end
